y $23$ koalas left in that forest? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718616 1072 #uuid "dd13a5ec-3f35-5991-8ad7-2b401a1a0073" 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718616 1073 true 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718616 1074 "The initial population is $P_0=543$ and the final population is $P=23$. A decrease of $2.9\\%$ per year means $r=-0.029$, with $t$ in years.\n\nUse the continuously compounded growth equation, isolate the exponential, take natural logarithms, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n23 &= 543e^{-0.029t} \\\\\ne^{-0.029t} &= \\frac{23}{543} \\\\\n\\ln\\left(e^{-0.029t}\\right) &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{23}{543}\\right) \\\\\n-0.029t &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{23}{543}\\right) \\\\\nt &= \\frac{\\ln\\left(\\frac{23}{543}\\right)}{-0.029} \\\\\nt &\\approx 109.02121 \\\\\nt &\\approx 109\\text{ years}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time is approximately $109$ years." 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718617 1080 "$71\\%$ per minute" 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718617 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718617 1083 #uuid "eaf162e4-3acf-5b86-93bc-5b7a27c58e2d" 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718618 1080 "$110$ years" 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718618 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718618 1083 #uuid "ebb1a0bf-293e-56a7-a6cb-2bd758c22d7b" 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718619 1080 "$112$ years" 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718619 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718619 1083 #uuid "ee77ff5d-d3ef-5a08-a02e-371a3435c0e2" 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718620 1080 "$116$ years" 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718620 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718620 1083 #uuid "ef913d26-3ead-5e56-a257-bb5a581f5780" 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718621 1068 #edb/ref 17592186718609 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718621 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718621 1071 "In a biology class, the teacher began the experiment with $34$ bacteria in a petri dish. After $7$ minutes, the number of bacteria increased to $2372$. What was the continuously compounded growth rate of the bacteria? Round your answer to the nearest percent.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718621 1072 #uuid "f6ec8216-66e5-56d8-884e-056c853ffa5a" 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718621 1073 true 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718621 1074 "The initial population is $P_0=34$, the final population is $P=2372$, and the elapsed time is $t=7$ minutes. The decimal rate $r$ is per minute.\n\nUse the continuously compounded growth equation, isolate the exponential, take natural logarithms, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= P_0e^{rt} \\\\\n2372 &= 34e^{7r} \\\\\ne^{7r} &= \\frac{2372}{34} \\\\\n\\ln\\left(e^{7r}\\right) &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{2372}{34}\\right) \\\\\n7r &= \\ln\\left(\\frac{2372}{34}\\right) \\\\\nr &= \\frac{\\ln\\left(\\frac{2372}{34}\\right)}{7} \\\\\nr &\\approx 0.6064469 \\\\\n100r &\\approx 60.64469\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConverting the decimal rate to a percentage and rounding to the nearest percent gives approximately $61\\%$ per minute." 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718622 1075 #edb/ref 17592186718597 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718622 1075 #edb/ref 17592186718612 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718622 1075 #edb/ref 17592186718618 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718622 1075 #edb/ref 17592186718619 13194139541591 17592186576411 true] [17592186718622 1075 #edb/ref 17592186718620 13194139541591 1759